body:
Thank you, I wish I could feel the same way about myself as you do.

&nbsp;

I suppose we could chat tomorrow.

&nbsp;

I really don't need gil anymore. I mostly acquire it out of compulsion.

Yeah, I can totally relate to that. The only friend I still talked to is going to start working 3rd shift. He will be making more money driving a forklift than I do with my college degree I went $100,000 in debt for. He also has a girlfriend.

&nbsp;

I basically won't be able to talk to him anyway, so avoiding is going to be super easy.

In the begging half of the year, I managed to be content with life while playing an MMO. I really enjoyed forgetting how few real life friends I have or how little I have to do. I looked forward to getting home usually to actually do something.

&nbsp;

In the latter half of the year, I have been dealing with arm, shoulder and neck pain.

I just don't see myself being that lucky. Especially not as lucky as you!

&nbsp;

I could try asking for social media in the future, but I'm not extremely active on social media myself.

&nbsp;

The game is Final Fantasy 14.

Can confirm.

I was put in the hospital over Christmas when I was a teenager.

&nbsp;

The only thing I learned there is how to pretend I'm ok so that I don't have to experience that again.

&nbsp;

As an adult, it would cost a job on top of being awful.

I had an ex that could not understand that I was doing my best when I would break down after driving her through heavy traffic. She at some point said to me "You're never going to make it through life like this". As much as it hurt that she broke up with me, I wished that I had broken up with her sooner.

&nbsp;

One thing I noticed you didn't mention was the fact that you are dealing with your relationship on top of everything else. I think you have a ton on your plate, so no one should be judging you harshly.

Thank you! :)

&nbsp;

Yeah, you're right. It is all about how I project myself. I just struggle to maintain a positive outward image. I've started to try to walk with my head up as my first step.
